## Facts (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/bucketB-java-zoneworld-summary.md` §"확인한 runtime 결함")
- `4d263e66b9` made `ZLinkJavaSocketReceivePoller.ensureRegistered()` register every socket with
  `POLLIN|POLLOUT|POLLCOMPLETION` (`.../runtime/binding/ZLinkJavaSocketReceivePoller.java:40-54`).
  SUB sockets have no completion queue; Core polling spec allows POLLCOMPLETION only for
  PAIR/DEALER/ROUTER/STREAM and ends unsupported source events with NOT_SUPPORTED/ENOTSUP
  (`core/doc/spec/core/05-polling.ko.md:85-90`, `:282-284`). Result: `ZLinkFanoutLocationRuntime`
  logged `fanout location tick failed` 3,262 / 3,006 / 2,144 times (~10 ms interval) in the three
  ZoneWorld zone nodes (`zlink-work/c016/logs/bucketB-java-zoneworld-current-prefix2/zone-node-1.log:19-39`,
  first stack at `SocketCore.completionOwner()`).
- The previous job prototyped: SUB poller registers `POLLIN` only (constructor flag in
  `ZLinkJavaSocketReceivePoller`, `ZLinkJavaSubscriberSocket` passing false) plus regression test
  `subscriberReadinessDoesNotClaimAnUnsupportedCompletionQueue` (passed), then reverted it under the
  one-cause rule. Re-implement it cleanly: the registration should follow the socket kind (only
  sockets that own a completion queue register POLLOUT|POLLCOMPLETION), matching how cpp/dotnet/node
  register SUB (`4644af9d03 framework/dotnet: poll SUB sockets without claiming completion ownership`
  is the dotnet precedent — read it for parity).
- Env: `cd framework/languages/java && TMPDIR=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-java flock -w7200 /tmp/zlink-jvm-gate.lock ./gradlew --no-daemon :zlink-framework-core:test --tests '*ReceiveOwner*' --tests '*Subscriber*'`;
  then a ZoneWorld zone-node smoke: `cd samples/java/ZoneWorld && ./run_sample.sh ZW-G1` with
  `ZLINK_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/hep7/project/zlink/.artifacts/wsl/install/zlink-core/0.17.0/lib/libzlink.so`
  and confirm `fanout location tick failed` count is 0 in the zone-node logs.

